+    """System prompt as cache-friendly blocks, ordered from never-changing to most-changing.
+
+    Prompt caching is a prefix hash, so what changes must come last:
+      1. INSTRUCTIONS: byte-identical for every athlete and day. Own cache_control marker.
+      2. profile: date, zones, goal, language. Changes at most daily.
+      3. one block per fact, append-only. save_fact only appends, so the previous
+         request's system prompt is an exact prefix of the next one. The marker sits
+         on the last block; the API looks back over earlier block boundaries (~20)
+         and finds the entry written by the previous call, so a new fact costs a
+         cache write of that one block instead of the whole prompt.
+    Keep facts strictly append-only and never put anything that varies after them.
+    """
+    blocks = [{"type": "text", "text": INSTRUCTIONS, "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}},
